# Heroku builds Dockerfile.heroku with the repository root as the build context. Send only what
# the image needs. Everything else stays out, above all sis_data/ (a logged-in SIS session and a
# student's progress) and .env (passwords and tokens).
#
# The Docker Compose images use their own lists: api/Dockerfile.dockerignore and web/.dockerignore.
*
!Dockerfile.heroku
!api/requirements.txt
!api/alembic.ini
!api/migrations/
!api/app/
# Not used by Dockerfile.heroku; listed so the Compose API image also builds with Docker's older builder.
!api/docker-entrypoint.sh
!data/catalog/
!data/programs/
!deploy/heroku/
!web/
web/node_modules
web/.next
web/e2e
web/coverage
web/*.tsbuildinfo
web/.env*
web/Dockerfile
web/.dockerignore
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
